# The Windows service's configuration: %ProgramData%\lowlat\lowlatd.env, the
# file lowlatd install creates and the host it starts reads. The file carries
# the signaling secret, so the folder is readable by the system account and
# administrators alone. The server is the public service when left empty.
KESSEL_WS_SERVER=
KESSEL_SESSION=

# The host's arguments, one string the C runtime's rules split, so quotes work
# here where a Linux unit splits on whitespace. For example:
# LOWLATD_ARGS=--name "Office PC"
# The display is captured unless --synth asks for the generator instead.
LOWLATD_ARGS=

# Reflexive servers, if the built-in pair are not the ones to use.
# LOWLAT_STUN=stun.l.google.com:19302,stun.cloudflare.com:3478
